  "school": "Price Action",
  "asset": "DJIA",
  "timeframe": "30min",
  "market_context": "Dow Jones had broken above the 50 EMA on the 30-minute chart, establishing bullish bias. Price retested the 50 EMA and formed a bullish engulfing candlestick, signaling a high-probability long entry. The 4-hour chart showed a prior double turning point supply zone as the long-term target.",
  "key_observation": "Price rejected the 50 EMA with a bullish engulfing pattern after breaking above it, confirming bullish momentum and triggering a long entry with tracking profits technique.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified bullish bias on the 30-minute chart after price broke above the 50 EMA and made a new high.",
    "Step 2: Noted price rejection of the 50 EMA via a bullish engulfing candlestick pattern, which served as the entry trigger.",
    "Step 3: Switched to the 4-hour chart to identify the long-term target: a supply zone that previously acted as a double turning point (rejected twice).",
    "Step 4: Entered a long position with stop-loss placed below the engulfing candle’s low.",
    "Step 5: Applied tracking profits technique: repositioning stop-loss below each new swing low after every Break of Structure (BOS) as price advanced."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "Tracking profits allows letting winners run by dynamically adjusting stop-loss under new swing lows after BOS, maximizing reward while preserving capital; confluence of HTF structure and LTF price action improves setup reliability.",
